{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-hom-set","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:glossary-hom-set","kind":"remark","title":"Hom-set","tags":["glossary","category-theory"],"defines":["hom-set"],"text":"glossary-hom-set.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:glossary-hom-set\"></a><p><strong><dfn class=\"defterm\" id=\"term-hom-set\">Hom-set</dfn>.</strong> For objects <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Y</code> in a category <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code>, the hom-set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Hom}_{\\mathbf{C}}(X, Y)</code> is the collection of all morphisms from <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code> to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Y</code>. It is also written <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}(X, Y)</code> or <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X \\to Y</code>. In a locally small category, each hom-set is a genuine set.</p>\n<p>When <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code> is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-linear, each hom-set carries the structure of an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module. Composition is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-bilinear.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/notation/glossary-hom-set.md","heading":"Remark","number":"30.2.1","page":"b/rem-glossary-hom-set","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
